Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]) and let $(M_a)_{a\ge1}$ be bounded operators on $H$ with

$$\sum_{a=1}^NM_a^*M_a\longrightarrow I\qquad\text{strongly as }N\to\infty .$$

Then:

(a) $\sum_{a\ge1}\|M_ax\|^2=\|x\|^2$ for every $x\in H$;

(b) for every positive trace-class $\rho$ the series $\sum_{a\ge1}M_a\rho M_a^*$ converges in trace norm to a positive trace-class operator $\Phi(\rho)$ with $\operatorname{tr}\Phi(\rho)=\operatorname{tr}\rho$;

(c) $\Phi$ extends uniquely to a linear positive map $\Phi:\mathcal S_1(H)\to\mathcal S_1(H)$ with $\operatorname{tr}\Phi(\rho)=\operatorname{tr}\rho$ for all trace-class $\rho$ and $\|\Phi(\rho)\|_1\le\|\rho\|_1$ for self-adjoint $\rho$; it maps density operators to density operators. No claim is made that every positive trace-preserving map has such a family.

Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a nonzero complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]), let $P$ be an orthogonal projection on $H$ ([[def-hilbert-orthogonal-projection]]) and let $\rho$ be a density operator with $p:=\operatorname{tr}(\rho P)>0$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]] clause (a)). Define the **selective update**
$$\rho_{P}:=\frac{P\rho P}{p}.$$
Then:

(a) $P\rho P$ is a positive trace-class operator with $\operatorname{tr}(P\rho P)=p$, so $\rho_{P}$ is a density operator;

(b) $\operatorname{tr}(\rho_{P}P)=1$ and
$$P\rho_{P}P=\rho_{P}=P\rho_{P}=\rho_{P}P;$$
in particular $\rho_{P}$ commutes with $P$ and is fixed by compression with $P$;

(c) if $Q$ is an orthogonal projection with $QP=0$, then $\operatorname{tr}(\rho_{P}Q)=0$ and $Q\rho_{P}Q=0$;

(d) if $\rho=T_{u,u}$ for a unit vector $u$ with $Pu\ne0$, where $T_{u,u}x=\langle x,u\rangle u$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-rank-one-operator-calculus]]), then $\rho_{P}=T_{Pu,Pu}/\|Pu\|^{2}$, the pure state of the normalized vector $Pu$; the value depends only on the ray of $Pu$, meaning its equivalence class of nonzero vectors under $x\sim y$ if $y=zx$ for some $z\in\mathbb C\setminus\{0\}$.

No physical interpretation of the update is asserted.

